      "id": 1,
      "text": "Asheboro was named after Governor Samuel Ashe and received its charter on Christmas Day 1796.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asheboro%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1889 the High Point, Randleman, Asheboro and Southern Railroad arrived, sparking prosperity and shifting the town center to Sunset Avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        23,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.asheboronc.gov/discover_asheboro/about_asheboro/history.php",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s industrial base grew from wood products to textile factories, with Acme-McCrary Hosiery Mills opening in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.achp.gov/preserve-america/community/asheboro-north-carolina",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Randolph County Courthouse, designated a Local Historic Landmark in 2008, stands as a centerpiece of Asheboro’s historic core.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.achp.gov/preserve-america/community/asheboro-north-carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Asheboro hosts the North Carolina Zoo, the state-owned wildlife park that opened in 1974 and draws visitors nationwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asheboro%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
